   "variant": "Arena Lauf 1 (alle Regeln)",
   "mode": "llm2",
   "guidance": "1. Select only regulations under which the component itself, or its installation on the vehicle, is approved. Do not select whole-vehicle regulations whose test object is the complete vehicle. These include frontal impact (R94, R137), side impact (R95, R135), external projections (R26), pedestrian safety (R127) and rear impact or fuel-system integrity. Their only link to the component is that it contributes to the vehicle's crash or projection performance. Select them only when the specification states the item is a separate technical unit or system approved under that regulation, or explicitly requests vehicle-type approval.\n2. Do not select regulations that govern a neighbouring object the component feeds, is fitted into, or merely activates. Three cases apply:\n(a) A light source (filament, gas-discharge or LED replacement lamp) is approved only under its light-source regulation (R37, R99, R128). Do not select the regulations for the lamps it is used in (e.g. R148, R149), the lighting-installation regulation (R48), or EMC (R10).\n(b) A system that only uses existing vehicle lamps or signals, such as flashing the direction indicators, does not bring in R48 or lamp regulations.\n(c) A replacement or aftermarket part with its own replacement-part regulation is approved under that regulation only. Examples are replacement silencing systems (R59, R92), replacement catalytic converters (R103) and replacement brake parts (R90). Do not add the vehicle-level emission or noise regulations (e.g. R40, R41, R47, R51, R83) whose limits the part must preserve, unless the specification explicitly requests vehicle approval.",
