   "variant": "Arena Lauf 2 (Runde 3)",
   "mode": "llm2",
   "guidance": "1. Separate vehicle-level regulations from component-level ones. Some regulations approve only a complete vehicle type. Examples: frontal and offset impact (R94, R137), side impact (R95), pedestrian protection (R127), external projections (R26), and vehicle exhaust emissions or noise of the whole vehicle type (e.g. R40 for motorcycle emissions). Do not select such a regulation just because the component influences or is checked during that vehicle test. Select it only in two cases. (a) It explicitly provides approval for the component itself as a component or separate technical unit, and the specified part falls within that scope. (b) The spec explicitly lists, as a function of the component, the specific protection that the regulation assesses, and the component is the dedicated vehicle structure that delivers it for the stated vehicle category. Example of (b): a front-end module whose stated function includes pedestrian lower-leg protection or low-speed impact protection; select the corresponding protection regulations. Being merely mounted on, near or inside such a structure, or being tested along with it, does not qualify. Aftermarket or replacement parts are approved under their dedicated component or replacement-part regulation, not under the vehicle-type regulation of the vehicle they fit.",
